#  Collection Framework is a group of classes and interfaces used to store and manage multiple data items
| Class                              | Interface                                                   |
| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Class is used to create objects.   | Interface is used to define rules that a class must follow. |
| Can have variables and methods.    | Can have method declarations.                               |
| Can create objects from a class.   | Cannot create objects from an interface.                    |
| A class can extend only one class. | A class can implement multiple interfaces.                  |
### Example
#### Interface
```java
interface Animal {
    void sound();
}```
#### Class
```java
class Dog implements Animal {
    public void sound() {
        System.out.println("Bark");
    }
}
### Real-Life Example      * **Interface** = Rules of a game.   * **Class** = A player who follows those rules.

